rvival depends on  them being rescued and holden decides to  rush out a statement broadcast it to  everyone which in his mind will keep  them safe as they're being taken onto  the martian ship he identifies himself  that they're survivors from the  canterbury and even though he doesn't  say it directly everything about his  statement makes it sound like mars is  responsible for killing their ship  on series miller heads to investigate  julie's apartment after feeling the  effects of the water rationing in his  own shower at first he doesn't find out  much she finds out she was arguing with  her father back and forth and that he  was threatening to sell her racing penis  the razorback later at the docks he  finds her connection to the scopuli and  at the same time he notices that local  gangsters have been abandoning their  territory on ceres also holden's message  has gotten out and has created real  tension between the belt and mars that  eventually leads to riots as the  oppressed belters take out their  frustrations against inners on the  station including havlock who gets  attacked by locals miller continues to  pursue julie despite his boss telling  him to back off he meets anderson dawes  who's a mysterious leader of the outer  planets alliance the opa who claims he  has no connection with julie or the  scopuli  on the doninger the survivors from the  cant are being interrogated by  lieutenant lopez since they don't really  know each other he tries to turn them  against each other to get information  and plants the seeds that naomi is an  opa sleeper agent this starts to feel  more likely when another stealth ship  appears and starts to pursue the  martians the ship's captain thinks it's  there to rescue naomi  on earth we meet the un undersecretary  general sadavir aaronright who was  pissed when he found out that christian  was torturing the belter who she does  interview again in a humane environment  but she still doesn't get any answers  and as he's being transferred to the  moon he allows himself to be killed by  not taking the high g injections  avasarala then manipulates the un  ambassador to mars who is her old family  friend she gives him bogus intel then  watches how the martians react to it  she's able to deduce that they weren't  involved in destroying the cant when  they scramble to see if any of their  stealth tech is missing mars does figure  out that the ambassador was used by  christian and then they ban him from the  planet he cuts ties with her and then  later he dies in an apparent suicide  avasarala now knows that someone who  wants to start a war is responsible for  the cant and she tries to send the ship  to the doninger to rescue holden and the  others  on taiko station you meet fred johnson  who's overseeing the construction of a  generationship for the mormons you see  that he's a no-nonsense kind of guy when  there's talk of replacing him over his  connections to the opa you also learn  that he's watching the situation with  the doninger closely  there holden's taken to the bridge and  refuses to take back his statement and  blame naomi for the cant what they  thought was one ship following them  turns out to be several and those start  to attack firing torpedoes at first this  isn't concerning as the doninger is a  flagship of the most technologically  advanced navy in the system but to their  surprise their pdc cannons aren't nearly  as effective as they should be and they  realize the attackers have some advanced  weaponry of their own this leads to an  intense and brutal close quarter battle  with the doninger being boarded shed  winds up as one of the casualties as his  head is blown clean off by a round  passing through the ship things look  dark for naomi alex and amos whose  compartment is now running out of air  and surrounded by vacuum when holden  tells the captain that these ships are  similar to the one that destroyed the  cant she has lopez take him to put him  on a shuttle because he's the only  witness to both attacks they fight their  way out and on the way lopez finally  explains what happened on phoebe station  which was mentioned a couple of times  during the interrogations the donager  had gone there after the research  station went dark for several weeks they  found no survivors and a clear cover-up  but don't know who was behind it or why  holden breaks away to rescue the others  not wanting to leave them behind and  they all make it to the hangar bay where  they're able to make it through heavy  fire to board the tachi before the  captain scuttles the doninger the crew  watch itself destruct as they make it  out on the corvette class light frigate  miller gets another big clue after the  series riot when he recognizes a dead  guy from julie's dating profile he turns  out to be a data broker who was hiding  his true identity and this leads miller  to discover a flight path for a ship  called the anubis havelock's in the  hospital and he's gonna survive and when  miller goes there we get an idea of how  his situation is starting to wear on him  as he's starting to become consumed with  julie in her case anderson dawes comes  clean admitting that she was opa he's  looking forward to and he offers up  havelock's attacker in return for any  information that miller comes across  miller does pass on the chance of  getting revenge and instead goes and  finds a guy whose ship duly chartered in  the time when she was getting more  involved with the opa who gives him a  lead while he's following up on that he  notices a robotic hamster in the shop he  went to and was reminded of the one that  was in her apartment when he goes back  there he finds a data cube he hides that  in his hat and then when he goes outside  he's abducted in a series of flashbacks  we learn about how fred johnson became  known as the butcher of anderson station  during his time as a colonel in the un  marine corps the part he played in that  atrocity made him infamous 